  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Which one of the following statements about <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\alpha\"></span>-particles, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\beta\"></span>-particles, and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\gamma\"></span> radiation is incorrect?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\beta\"></span>-particles are always emitted together with a neutrino.</li>\n<li data-label=\"B\">When <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\beta\"></span>-particles travel a certain distance through air, fewer ions are produced than when <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\gamma\"></span> radiation travels through the same distance in air.</li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\alpha\"></span>-particles travel slower in vacuum than gamma radiation. </li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\gamma\"></span> radiation is undeflected in a magnetic field.</li>\n</ol>"
  },
